{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLOctaveShift\/number","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLOctaveShift"]]},"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"symbolKind":"property","roleHeading":"Instance Property","role":"symbol","title":"number","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL14MXLOctaveShiftV6numberAA14MXLNumberLevelVSgvp","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"number","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL14MXLNumberLevelV","text":"MXLNumberLevel","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}]},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Distinguishes multiple octave shifts occurring simultaneously."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxloctaveshift\/number"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"number","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNumberLevel","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL14MXLNumberLevelV","text":"MXLNumberLevel","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps to the MusicXML "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"number"},{"type":"text","text":" attribute."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNumberLevel":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNumberLevel","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLNumberLevel"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Slurs, tuplets, and many other features can be concurrent and overlap within a single musical part. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"number-level entity distinguishes up to 16 concurrent objects of the same type when the objects overlap in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"MusicXML document order. Values greater than 6 are usually only needed for music with a large number of divisi"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"staves in a single part, or if there are more than 6 cross-staff arpeggios in a single measure. When a number-"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"level value is implied, the value is 1 by default."}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLNumberLevel","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnumberlevel","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLNumberLevel"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLOctaveShift/number":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLOctaveShift\/number","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"number","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Distinguishes multiple octave shifts occurring simultaneously."}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxloctaveshift\/number","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"number"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL14MXLNumberLevelV","text":"MXLNumberLevel"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLOctaveShift":{"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The octave shift type indicates where notes are shifted up or down from their true pitched values because of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"printing difficulty. Thus a treble clef line noted with 8va will be indicated with an octave-shift down from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the pitch data indicated in the notes. A size of 8 indicates one octave; a size of 15 indicates two octaves."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLOctaveShift","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxloctaveshift","title":"MXLOctaveShift","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLOctaveShift"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLOctaveShift"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL"}}}